CITIZENSHIP, ETHNICITY AND RELIGION
Khalkh ethnic group accounts for 83.8 percent of the population, which is an increase of 1.4 percentage
points from the previous census. The percentage of Kazakh ethnic group in the total population is 3.8
percent, second only to the Khalkhs. The proportion of Durvud, Bayad, and Buriad ethnic groups have
been declining since 2010. In terms of the location, the Khalkh ethnic group is prevalent in all aimags
and the capital city. Bayan-Ulgii (0.9 percent), Uvs (13.6 percent) and Khovd (28.1 percent) have the
lowest percentage of Khalkh ethnic group in the total population of the aimags respectively. In contrast,
in Bayankhongor, Gobi-Altai, Dundgovi, Zavkhan and Uvurkhangai aimags, more than 99 percent of the
aimag population are Khalkhs.
The number of foreign nationals residing in Mongolia for 6 months or more increased by 37.4
percent or 6 098 people from 2010 to 22 418. The number of stateless persons has decreased from 71

